    "review_conclusion": {
      "canonical_alignment": "Final configuration and extension draft match; formal player content, effect, formulas and tables match the approved canonical values and stated conditions.",
      "inventory_and_indices": "Map has the one blessing object, three exact trait variants and seven exact bindings for combatknife_p1, dual_shivs_p1 and ogryn_club_p2. Each binding points to its real Mark template import/append and corresponding formal variant page. Shared blessing/melee indices and all three weapon reverse pages link to this entry and list the actual Marks.",
      "tier_and_wrapper": "All three own tier files give I–IV .01/.02/.03/.04 per effective stack and formatter percent-plus; each wrapper clones the activated parent, selects its actual child, and clones that child. Child effective cap is five (six raw slots include reserved placeholder); chance is n*p, with no additional inferred clamp.",
      "first_effect_and_event_batch": "Starts at zero effective stacks. The hit that queues a new layer is resolved first; the child handles all queued events before the parent adds one layer per qualifying hit. Same-batch target checks use the pre-batch stack count. Multi-target hits can add multiple layers; no combo-step predicate is implemented.",
      "target_action_lifetime": "Child requires live target and breed then excludes captain, monster, ogryn and cultist_captain tags; this is not a geometry/height test. Heavy action matrix, heavy push-follow exceptions, light specials, pure push and thrown projectile exclusions match all seven bound Marks. Shared timer removes one layer after each five-second idle interval; qualifying events including cap hits refresh it. Switching away stops held-gated checks while timer continues; actual parent destruction removes its controlled children.",
      "raw_and_formula": "I–IV full English and Traditional Chinese formatter reconstructions match the exact RAW keys/hashes. Chained Heavy Hit is classified as documentation not covering the exact combo-state condition, not as a proven translation error; human-sized is likewise not a geometric rule. The blanket claim that no other potential triggers activate on Instakill is an explicit mismatch because generic on_hit/on_kill events still dispatch; receiving effects retain their own predicates. IV example at n=2 is 8%, then parent adds one stack; a later separate event at n=3 is 12%.",
      "image": "All three actual trait items use item.icon content/ui/textures/icons/traits/weapon_trait_195; official attachment matches the reviewed source/public image receipt. ID/path and attachment URL are not conflated.",
      "punctuation_delta": "Rechecked final LOCALIZATION_COMPARISON: complete IV Chinese RAW line ends cleanly; the sentence explaining shared format and static reconstruction is a separate paragraph, without the prior terminal full stop plus semicolon."
    },
